   239	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   240	    """
   241	    Flood-fill a multicolor half-enclosure and radiate outward using wall-function colors.
   242	
   243	    Input structure:
   244	    - Background is the most common color.
   245	    - A single 8-connected wall sprite is built from three fixed wall colors: blue side, red side, and orange bridge.
   246	    - A non-wall seed blob sits inside the enclosure; other non-wall non-seed pixels are singleton obstacles.
   247	
   248	    Rule:
   249	    - Fill spreads through background cells reachable from the seed, first inside the enclosure and then out through the opening.
   250	    - The two wall endpoints project different outside boundary rays according to endpoint color:
   251	      red keeps the original slanted ray, blue projects a straight ray along the opening direction.
   252	    - Obstacles preserve their colors and erase fill behind them along the global radiate direction.
   253	
   254	    Key insight:
   255	    - The wall must be parsed as one multicolor object, then each endpoint's color determines which kind of
   256	      boundary ray constrains the exterior fill region.
   257	    """
   258	    return _solve(grid, functional_walls=True)
